    "MoViNet offers several pretrained models, and we tested three of their base versions: A0, A1, and A2. These models were trained on the Kinetics-600 dataset, which does not include three of our targeted exercises—plank, barbell biceps curl, and shoulder press. As a result, the accuracy evaluation was conducted only on the remaining five exercises from our assignment dataset.\n",
    "\n",
    "To ensure that each model captured a full repetition of an exercise, we processed 50 frames per video, selecting every third frame.\n",
    "\n",
    "Model Performance:\n",
    "\n",
    "* A0 → 83.33% accuracy (15 min runtime)\n",
    "* A1 → 84.8% accuracy (50 min runtime)\n",
    "* A2 → 91.1% accuracy (2-hour runtime)\n",
    "\n",
    "Among the three models, A2 delivered the highest accuracy. However, for the next phase of our work, we will use A0 due to its significantly lower computational cost and shorter runtime. While A2 provides better classification performance, the trade-off in efficiency makes A0 a more practical choice for iterative testing and further development. Future refinements, such as fine-tuning on our dataset or using model distillation techniques, could help bridge the performance gap while maintaining efficiency."
